this information is from north east  derbyshire district council  north east derbyshire district council  is proud to announce  that it will have  an engagement event for deaf people who  are residents in that area  in northeast derbyshire  this follows  them signing the bsl charter  in september 2019  where the council committed to all five  pledges  this event will be an opportunity for  deaf residents  to come together  at  drumfield  leisure centre  the event will showcase leisure services  with staff presenting information  about their leisure services what they  provide and how people can be involved  there will also be an opportunity for a  tour of the leisure centre  as well as asking questions of the  this event will highlight the positive  steps that the council's done  after signing the bsl charter  to  improve and assist deaf residents  at the event there will also be a  present presentation from sound  solutions  demonstrating their video relay service  the account has now agreed this  at its leisure centers  and head office  at wingerworth  which means deaf people  or deaf customers are able to contact  them  via sign language interpreters  this event will be held on friday the  8th of july  from half past 12 to 3 p.m  at drum field leisure centre  that is the civic center  in dronfield  the postcode  is s  18  1  p d  when you arrive at the event there will  be a light buffet available  between half past 12 and 1.  at the event there will be a bsl  interpreter available  if you have any questions  or any special requirements  please contact  amar  bashir  his email address is  a a m a r dot b a s h i r  at  n e hyphen  d d e r b y s h i r e dot gov dot u k
 

